body:
Below is a user, I need to set a disjunctive facet on Skills.SkillName (eg where Skills.SkillName = 'SQL' OR 'Accounting')

{"FirstName" : "John",
"LastName" : "Smith",
"JobFunction" : "Information Technology",
"Skills" : \[{
"SkillID" : "2vRdiqCOE2XBDS3nsS1LA",
"SkillName" : "SQL",
"SkillRating" : 3
}, {
"SkillID" : "WEPMtg3JkU2xlpmgmvkYQ",
"SkillName" : "Accounting",
"SkillRating" : 4
}, {
"SkillID" : "d9c514035a554a5d8d99c411e43b683d",
"SkillName" : "Leadership",
"SkillRating" : 4
}]}

Ive attempted a lot of different things, but here is what I think makes sense:

`var preselectedCategories = ['SQL', 'Accounting'];
var search = instantsearch({
    appId: 'appid',
    apiKey: 'api',
    indexName: 'UserActivity',
    searchParameters: {
        disjunctiveFacetsRefinements: {
            Skills: {
                SkillName: preselectedCategories
            }
        }
    }
});`

Documentation is definitely lacking on this so any help will be greatly appreciated. Thanks!
